  "name": "Mijikenda ngoma (Giriama and Digo drum-song, sengenya)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Drum-song and dance music of the Mijikenda peoples of the Kenyan coast and its hinterland, among them the Giriama of Kilifi and the Digo of Kwale, performed at weddings, funerals and community celebrations; named dances include sengenya. Ensembles combine several drums with kayamba raft rattles and, in some dances, the chivoti transverse flute, under a leader's songs answered by a chorus. The membrane-drum card stands in for the drum set.",
